(23710, ' 219 Sydenham Rd', '219-sydenham-rd', 18383, 18207, NULL, 'Piled foundations and RC frame (W12TBC)', '<p>The existing site is home to a three bedroom</p><p>detached property that is in need of extensive</p><p>structural remedial works or replacement.</p><p>This statement should be read in conjunction with</p><p>the planning statement prepared by First Plan</p><p>submitted as part of the original approved planning</p><p>application. DC/17/104391. This VOC application is for</p><p>minor amendments to the front and rear principle</p><p>elevations and wall details and changing the</p><p>proposed accommodation from 5 units (1x3 bed and</p><p>4 x 2 bed) to 6 units (1x3 bed, 2 x 1 bed and 3 x 2 bed)</p><p>to improve the viability of the site.</p><p><br></p><p>Location</p><p>The site is located at 219 Sydenham Road (A212)</p><p>between Lower Sydenham and Sydenham. The site</p><p>is almost equidistant (apx 0.5km) from Sydenham</p><p>and Lower Sydenham railway stations. It is well</p><p>served with local amenities close to a number of</p><p>open green spaces and parks. There are very good</p><p>bus services along Sydenham Road, with stops close</p><p>by in both directions.</p><p>The site is currently occupied by an poorly sited 3</p><p>bedroom detached family home which is out of</p><p>scale (low) for its siting and proximity to this busy</p><p>main road.</p>', 4, 24, 0, '2023-05-02', '2023-11-30', 0, '2023-05-02 15:27:47', '219 Sydenham Rd', '', 'London', 'SE26 5HF', 4, 2, 0, '0', 0),
