(23799, 'Bedwas Welfare Project ', 'bedwas-welfare-project', 21951, 22201, NULL, 'Nauire ', '<p>Nuaire plan to make a number of internal building and façade changes at its warehouse and distribution centre in Bedwas, Caerphilly. The proposed changes are largely considered non-structural although a number of changes forming additional doorways and windows may require steelwork review and adjustment thereof. </p><p><br></p><p>Through this RFQ we aim to understand how you would propose to offer the services using the best balance of cost, risk, safety, efficiency, visibility, and lead times. </p><p><br></p><p>The plans are to modernise some of the existing office and through traffic spaces and create new welfare, toilet and changing facilities. In essence that means: </p><p><br></p><p>Ground Floor </p><p>1. Modernising the existing entrance and stairwell.</p><p>2. Repurposing an existing space to a new welfare facility. </p><p>3. Creating new suite of individual toilet facilities and a handwash location. </p><p>4. Creating a new entrance foyer. </p><p>5. Creating a new colleague throughfare foyer. </p><p>6. Creating a new first aid and occupational health room. </p><p>7. Creating a new male and female changing facility. </p><p>8. Creating a new PPE drying room. First Floor </p><p>9. Reconditioning the existing operations managers office. </p><p>10. Reconditioning the existing transport planning office into CI Opex Office. </p><p>11. Repurposing the existing welfare facility into a Project Room. </p><p>12. Creating a new training room on the first floor. </p><p>13. Creating a new safety partition on the first floor, Supply and install a new small kitchen area and modernising existing structure interfaces. </p><p>14. Creating a new Office on the first floor. Each area is covered further on, in more detail within the scope of works. </p><p>The type of building works we have envisaged within the project can be summarised as: </p><p>1. Plumbing and connection works to main sewer. </p><p>2. Electrical. </p><p>3. Flooring. </p><p>4. Suspended Ceiling.</p><p> 5. Heating (Boiler). </p><p>6. Ventilation ductwork.</p><p> 7. Cladding. </p><p>8. Door and Window Fitting. </p><p>9. Stud Walling. </p><p>10. Insulation and Soundproofing. </p><p>11. Plastering. </p><p>12. Carpentry. </p><p>13. Steelwork. </p><p>14. Painting and Decorating</p>', 11, 22, 0, '2023-09-04', '2023-12-15', 0, '2023-07-28 08:53:03', 'Nuaire Home Ventilation Ltd', 'Block A', 'Caerphilly', 'cf83 1na ', 3, 3, 0, '0', 0),
(23800, '30 Arklow Road', '30-arklow-road', 18383, 21675, NULL, 'W12', '<p>10 Arches</p>', 4, 25, 0, '2023-08-22', '2023-12-27', 0, '2023-08-01 08:29:40', 'Arches 234 to 243', '30 Arklow Road', 'London', 'SE14 6EB', 0, 0, 0, '0', 0),
(23801, '8 Oldbury Place', '8-oldbury-place', 21685, 22207, NULL, 'L1278', '<p>8 Oldbury Place once formed part of the larger terraced house known as 38 Nottingham Place. A number of extensions were added to the open space between the two buildings over time, resulting in a rather haphazard collection of accumulations over four floor levels. These included extensions and internal terraces at multiple levels. Of note is one part of 38 Nottingham Place that oversails 8 Oldbury Place in the form of a flying freehold. Immediately to the north of the site is located The Princess Grace Hospital, occupying the whole of the northern end of the mews. The hospital also includes 9 Oldbury Place and thus shares a party wall with the property.</p>', 4, 23, 0, '2023-10-29', '2024-05-27', 3, '2023-08-01 12:17:39', '8 Oldbury Place', '', 'London', 'W1U 5PG', 4, 4, 0, '0', 0),
